  "reason": "The best result so far is config_041 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc=0.725). The evidence clearly shows transformer aggregation > avgpool (+0.019) and scvi_n200 >> scgpt (+0.205), confirming the current best configuration. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the transformer aggregation benefit is specific to the ViT-L image encoder or generalizable. Config_015 changes only the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l → resnet50) while holding all other proven-optimal settings (scvi_n200, transformer, weighted, multiprofile, multimodal) constant. This single-variable test will clarify whether the image encoder choice is a critical factor or whether the transformer aggregation provides robust gains across encoders. If resnet50 performs comparably, it broadens the search; if it drops significantly, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is essential and we can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning around the config_041 neighborhood. With 4 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information single step that reduces uncertainty about an important design axis without abandoning the proven direction."
}

